    "body": "## Summary\n- add atomic versioned backup bundles for PostgreSQL/PostGIS and encrypted attachment objects\n- add SHA-256 manifest verification and restrictive backup permissions\n- add a guarded restore command that cannot overwrite the active database and only restores attachments into isolated recovery paths\n- add an executable CI restore drill that seeds database + attachment markers, backs them up, restores into isolated targets, and verifies database content, attachment bytes and PostGIS\n- add an operator runbook covering off-host durability, encryption-key recovery, restore verification and disaster-recovery boundaries\n\n## Safety / launch boundary\n- no Flyway migration: this slice changes operational recovery tooling, not application schema\n- restore requires explicit `DOFAST_RESTORE_CONFIRM=RESTORE_DOFAST_BACKUP`\n- restore refuses the active `POSTGRES_DB` and fails if the target database already exists\n- attachment restore is restricted to `/var/lib/dofast/restore/*` or `/tmp/dofast-restore-*`\n- backup bundles intentionally do not contain DB passwords, JWT/Stripe secrets or the attachment encryption key\n- off-host storage, RPO/RTO policy, backup-age alerting and secret-manager recovery remain environment/operator responsibilities\n\n## Validation required before merge\n- API Maven verify\n- web test/audit/lint/build\n- production Compose contract\n- full containers/runtime smoke including the new real backup/restore drill\n- exact latest-head and unchanged-base verification before merge\n\nMerge only with a merge commit after every latest-head check is complete and green.",
